--- loop page
---
title: "Loop playback"
description: "Repeat the in/out range or the whole timeline while you watch and adjust."
---

import AtAGlance from '@components/AtAGlance.astro';

Loop keeps playback going round, so you can watch a passage over and over while you adjust it.

<AtAGlance where="The Loop button in the toolbar" />

## Turn Loop on

Click **Loop**, the repeat button at the end of the transport in the toolbar. The button is dimmed while Loop is off and full strength while it's on. Click it again to turn Loop off.

Loop has no menu item and no key. It's off when a window opens, it's set for each window on its own, and it isn't saved with the project.

## What it repeats

| What's set | What Loop repeats |
| --- | --- |
| An [in/out range](/timeline/in-out-range/) | The range |
| No range, or a range of no length | The whole timeline |

--- speed page
A ramp that slows a clip down makes it play less of its file, so it can stop reaching speech it played before.

A caption whose speech the clip no longer reaches is removed. A word caption page that's only partly reached keeps the words that still play, and its text is cut to match.

## Newly revealed speech

When a speed-up or a ramp makes the clip play further into its file, the new part gets no captions. [Generate Captions](/captions/generate-captions/) again to caption it.

## Neighbouring captions

A moved caption is cut back where it would run into a caption that didn't move. One that would start inside such a caption, or end up shorter than a frame, is removed.

## Good to know

- Only speed and ramp edits move captions. A trim, slip or split leaves them where they are.
- [Retime Range](/speed/retime-range/) works differently. It stretches or squeezes a text clip in the range along with everything else, and Frame Job won't retime a range that touches a caption page with timed words.
- Frame Job checks every new place before it commits. If they don't all work out, the speed edit goes through on its own and the captions stay where they were.

## Related

- [Captions are text clips](/captions/how-captions-work/)
- [Edit captions](/captions/edit-captions/)
